<section class="section section--alt" id="files" aria-labelledby="files-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">// open anything you can <code>ls</code></p>
    <h2 id="files-title">It opens your files itself.</h2>
    <p class="section__lede">
      Images and models go straight into the same GPU pipeline. Text gets an editor tab, music gets a player
      tab. From the shell, from Finder, or from a Lua module.
    </p>

    <ul class="grid grid--4 kinds">
      <li class="kind">
        <svg class="kind__icon c-blue" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"></rect><circle cx="9" cy="10" r="2"></circle><path d="M21 16l-5-5-9 9"></path></svg>
        <h3>Images</h3>
        <p>Pan and zoom in a GPU viewer.</p>
        <p class="exts">png jpg gif bmp tga psd hdr</p>
      </li>
      <li class="kind">
        <svg class="kind__icon c-purple" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 2l9 5v10l-9 5-9-5V7z"></path><path d="M12 22V12M21 7l-9 5-9-5"></path></svg>
        <h3>3D models</h3>
        <p>Drag to orbit, wheel to zoom.</p>
        <p class="exts">obj stl ply</p>
      </li>
      <li class="kind">
        <svg class="kind__icon c-green" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 7l-5 5 5 5M16 7l5 5-5 5M14 4l-4 16"></path></svg>
        <h3>Text &amp; code</h3>
        <p>Built-in editor with syntax colouring, undo, and a <span class="run">▶ Run</span> button for scripts.</p>
        <p class="exts">txt md json lua py sh …</p>
      </li>
      <li class="kind">
        <svg class="kind__icon c-yellow" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18V5l12-2v13"></path><circle cx="6" cy="18" r="3"></circle><circle cx="18" cy="16" r="3"></circle></svg>
        <h3>Music</h3>
        <p>A player tab with title, artist and a seekable progress bar.</p>
        <p class="exts">mp3 m4a wav flac aiff aac</p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <h3 class="split__title">Every file name is a link</h3>
        <p>
          Any path printed in the terminal — by <code>ls</code>, <code>git status</code>, a compiler error — is
          underlined and clickable. Folders <code>cd</code> into themselves.
        </p>
        <dl class="keys">
          <div><dt>click</dt><dd>select it</dd></div>
          <div><dt>click again · <kbd>⏎</kbd></dt><dd>open it</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>⌘</kbd> + click</dt><dd>open instantly</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>tab</kbd> on empty prompt</dt><dd>select the nearest file name</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>tab</kbd> / arrows</dt><dd>move between names</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>esc</kbd></dt><dd>let go</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="default-app">
        <div class="menu" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="menu__head"><b>terminal</b></div>
          <div class="menu__item">About terminal</div>
          <div class="menu__sep"></div>
          <div class="menu__item is-hot">Make terminal the Default App…</div>
          <div class="menu__item">Restore Previous Defaults</div>
          <div class="menu__sep"></div>
          <div class="menu__item">Quit terminal <span>⌘Q</span></div>
        </div>
        <h3 class="split__title">Make it the default app</h3>
        <p>
          One menu item makes terminal the default app for every type above. Your previous defaults are saved
          first, so <em>Restore Previous Defaults</em> puts everything back.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
